<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 222)</h2>
<p><b>Record the Session.</b> The staying-sane tool for the five-people-talking review.</p>
<ul>
<li><b>Notes ▸ Record the Session (⌥⌘V)</b> records the room — your mic, the call audio in it — while Asobi logs what's on screen the whole time: every frame, every clip change.</li>
<li>Stop, and the on-device transcript becomes <b>session minutes</b>: everything said, in order, placed under the shot that was up when it was said. Grouped by clip, saved with the session, exported with your notes.</li>
<li>Deliberately unattributed — it records one room and doesn't pretend to know who spoke. The attributed record is still everyone's own notes, which sync live.</li>
<li>A red <b>RECORDING SESSION</b> badge shows throughout, and audio never leaves your machine.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
